  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A Face operation now accepts \"Do not touch\" picks. The Boundary group of the Geometry tab shows \"Pick protected\" for a Face operation.\n- At each cut level, the Face generator gets the cutter-centre keep-out of the protected items. The keep-out covers flutes, shank and holder, plus the clearance, for each tip height from the level up to the clearance plane.\n- The generator cuts each row short at the keep-out. It uses the same interval law that clips rows at bridged holes (`face_holes::pieces`).\n- Where a row is cut short, or where a row-end step (sharp or blended) crosses the keep-out, the facer links over the keep-out at the clearance plane: up, across, plunge.\n- The existing rapid router raises a link that must go higher. The existing `verify_avoid` check and the post gate read every Face move.\n- A level with no row left is skipped. A path note tells this.\n- When no level is left, the generator refuses the operation and names the protected items. The post is blocked.\n- A path note tells that the material beside the protected items stays unfaced.\n- Without protected items, the Face path is the same as before, move for move.\n- The refusal text for an unsupported kind and the MCP tool text now name Face.\n\nNew code:\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/face_keep.rs`: the per-level clip, the step test and the notes.\n- `machining2d::face_over_kept` and `machining2d::FaceKeep`. `face_over` calls `face_over_kept` with `None`.\n\n## Cause\n\n`do_not_touch_applies` held only 2D Offset and 3D Pocket. The Face generator did not read the protected items.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins:\n- `crates/app/tests/do_not_touch_face.rs`\n  - `face_do_not_touch_keeps_full_tool_clear_of_protected_face`: a Face at Cut Z 20 runs over a tower. With the tower top protected (clearance 1.5 mm), no sample of any move below the tower top comes nearer than 4.5 mm (flute radius 3 + 1.5). Verify is clean. The post writes NC.\n  - `face_do_not_touch_refuses_an_impossible_cut_by_name_and_blocks_the_post`: the plate top is protected with a 16 mm clearance. Generate refuses with \"Do not touch\" and \"plate\" in the text. The post is refused and writes no file.\n  - `face_without_protection_keeps_its_toolpath`: protection changes the path. After undo of the protection, the path is the same as the first path, move for move.\n- `crates/motion/tests/face_keep.rs`\n  - `empty_keepout_is_face_over_to_the_byte` (4 cases: sharp, blended, single level, staged).\n  - `rows_and_steps_keep_out_of_the_keepout_and_link_over_it` (sharp and blended).\n  - `a_keepout_over_every_row_refuses_by_name`.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/do_not_touch.rs`\n  - `face_op_shows_pick_protected_button` (new).\n  - `unsupported_op_shows_do_not_touch_note_without_pick_button`: the note text now names Face.\n\nRed before the fix: both app pins failed on `upstream/main` 174584111 with `'Do not touch' is supported on 2D Offset and 3D Pocket operations only so far - clear it on Face`.\n\nMutations (each one red, then green after restore):\n- Remove the `step_clear` guard in `face.rs`: `rows_and_steps_keep_out_of_the_keepout_and_link_over_it` fails.\n- Make `face_keep::level` ignore the keep-out: two motion pins fail.\n- Pass `None` for the keep-out in `generate.rs`: all three app pins fail. (Verify finds the avoid hit, so the safety net blocks the post too.)\n\nGate:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 280 steps, 0 failed (`ui suites: lib` 1425 passed).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Heavy lanes\n\n- Head: `b38f0c12f33ec6b2e1c8e0ea7d59c20c74130db4` (unchanged; no merge or code push).\n- Base: `upstream/main` at `054c1e24bb15f27fee5f022ab454384c951e8e64`, fetched before the run.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: GREEN. 242 steps, 0 failed. Exit 0.\n- Lanes: 1 release build, 37 motion heavy steps, 204 app heavy steps.\n- Four known-fail checks were red as expected. The tool counted them as OK: #1950 (three checks), #2849 (one check).\n- App heavy included `example_catalog` and `golden_cl`. These ran with the heavy lane's ignored-test selection.\n- The worktree is clean. No code, golden or recorded program changed.\n- No new pin or mutation was needed. This round had no code findings. The reviewed pins and mutation results above still apply.\n- This round did not repeat quick, clippy or the regular debug catalog suite. The requested work was the owed heavy run.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A Face laid along an open boundary (a turned frame) with protected items. The keep-out turns with the region, but no test covers it.\n- A tilted (3+2) Face with protected items.\n- A protected edge chain on a Face (the app pin uses a face pick).\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2831 (draft, `needs-rework`, `conflicts`) changes other lines of the Face arm in `generate.rs` (the `blend_radius` field). It touches the same file, different lines; whichever merges second refreshes.\n- Several open PRs touch `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs` and `crates/motion/src/machining2d/mod.rs` in other functions or other lines.\n\n## Decision\n\n`docs/decisions/3343-face-do-not-touch.md`.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: \"Do not touch\" now works on Face operations: the rows stay clear of each protected face or edge by the clearance, and a cut that cannot stay clear is refused with the item named.\n\nFixes #3343\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
